Senior-level question
Q: Is val thread-safe?
"val prevents reassignment of the binding, but it does not automatically make a
referenced mutable object thread-safe. Thread safety depends on the object's
mutability and how it is accessed. Immutable values are generally easier to
share safely across concurrent operations."

Q: Is lazy val thread-safe?
"Scala's lazy val initialization mechanism coordinates concurrent
access so that the initializer is evaluated once after successful initialization.
However, thread safety of the object returned by the lazy val is a separate concern."